1	# Advanced ClaudePoint Usage
2	
3	This guide covers advanced topics for power users and edge cases.
4	
5	## Multi-Project Setup
6	
7	To manage multiple projects simultaneously, create separate MCP server entries:
8	
9	```json
10	{
11	  "mcpServers": {
12	    "claudepoint-web": {
13	      "command": "claudepoint",
14	      "env": {
15	        "CLAUDEPOINT_PROJECT_DIR": "/path/to/web-project"
16	      }
17	    },
18	    "claudepoint-api": {
19	      "command": "claudepoint",
20	      "env": {
21	        "CLAUDEPOINT_PROJECT_DIR": "/path/to/api-project"
22	      }
23	    }
24	  }
25	}
26	```
27	
28	## Hooks Advanced Configuration
29	
30	### Custom Trigger Patterns
31	
32	Configure hooks for specific workflows:
33	
34	```bash
35	# Enable specific triggers
36	claudepoint hooks enable before_bash_commands
37	claudepoint hooks enable before_file_operations
38	
39	# Set auto-changelog for detailed tracking
40	claudepoint hooks set-changelog true
41	```
42	
43	### Hook Configuration File
44	
45	The `.checkpoints/hooks.json` file:
46	
47	```json
48	{
49	  "enabled": true,
50	  "auto_changelog": true,
51	  "triggers": {
52	    "before_bulk_edit": {
53	      "enabled": true,
54	      "tools": ["MultiEdit"],
55	      "description": "Safety checkpoint before bulk file edits"
56	    },
57	    "before_major_write": {
58	      "enabled": false,
59	      "tools": ["Write"],
60	      "description": "Safety checkpoint before major file writes"
61	    },
62	    "before_bash_commands": {
63	      "enabled": false,
64	      "tools": ["Bash"],
65	      "description": "Safety checkpoint before executing bash commands"
66	    },
67	    "before_file_operations": {
68	      "enabled": false,
69	      "tools": ["Edit", "MultiEdit", "Write"],
70	      "description": "Safety checkpoint before any file modification"
71	    }
72	  }
73	}
74	```
75	
76	## Performance Optimization
77	
78	### Large Projects
79	
80	For projects with many files or large binaries:
81	
82	1. **Update ignore patterns**:
83	   ```json
84	   {
85	     "ignorePatterns": [
86	       "*.mp4", "*.mov", "*.zip",
87	       "vendor/", "cache/", "tmp/",
88	       "*.sqlite", "*.db"
89	     ]
90	   }
91	   ```
92	
93	2. **Increase Node.js memory**:
94	   ```bash
95	   NODE_OPTIONS="--max-old-space-size=4096" claudepoint create
96	   ```
97	
98	3. **Use force include for specific files**:
99	   ```json
100	   {
101	     "forceInclude": [".env.example", "docs/**/*.md"]
102	   }
103	   ```
104	
105	## Incremental Checkpoint Tuning
106	
107	### Custom Chain Length
108	
109	Adjust incremental checkpoint behavior:
110	
111	```json
112	{
113	  "incremental": {
114	    "enabled": true,
115	    "fullSnapshotInterval": 10,  // More incremental checkpoints
116	    "maxChainLength": 50          // Longer chains for maximum efficiency
117	  }
118	}
119	```
120	
121	### Force Full Checkpoints
122	
123	For major milestones:
124	
125	```bash
126	# Force a full checkpoint
127	claudepoint create --full --description "Version 1.0 release"
128	
129	# Via Claude
130	"Create a full checkpoint for the v1.0 release"
131	```
132	
133	## Working Directory Issues
134	
135	### macOS/Linux
136	
137	If ClaudePoint operates in the wrong directory:
138	
139	```json
140	{
141	  "mcpServers": {
142	    "claudepoint": {
143	      "command": "/usr/local/bin/node",
144	      "args": ["/usr/local/lib/node_modules/claudepoint/bin/claudepoint.js"],
145	      "env": {
146	        "CLAUDEPOINT_PROJECT_DIR": "/Users/username/project"
147	      }
148	    }
149	  }
150	}
151	```
152	
153	### Windows
154	
155	For Windows-specific path issues:
156	
157	```json
158	{
159	  "mcpServers": {
160	    "claudepoint": {
161	      "command": "C:\\Program Files\\nodejs\\node.exe",
162	      "args": ["C:\\Users\\USER\\AppData\\Roaming\\npm\\node_modules\\claudepoint\\bin\\claudepoint.js"],
163	      "env": {
164	        "CLAUDEPOINT_PROJECT_DIR": "C:\\Projects\\MyProject"
165	      }
166	    }
167	  }
168	}
169	```
170	
171	## Development Workflow Patterns
172	
173	### Feature Branch Pattern
174	
175	```bash
176	# 1. Create checkpoint before new feature
177	claudepoint create --description "Before user-profile feature"
178	
179	# 2. Work on feature...
180	
181	# 3. Create checkpoint at milestone
182	claudepoint create --description "User profile UI complete"
183	
184	# 4. If something breaks
185	claudepoint restore "user-profile"
186	```
187	
188	### Experimentation Pattern
189	
190	```bash
191	# 1. Checkpoint current stable state
192	claudepoint create --description "Stable - all tests passing"
193	
194	# 2. Try risky refactoring
195	# ... make changes ...
196	
197	# 3. If it doesn't work out
198	claudepoint restore "stable" --dry-run  # Preview first
199	claudepoint restore "stable"            # Restore
200	```
201	
202	### Debug Pattern
203	
204	```bash
205	# 1. Create checkpoint before debugging
206	claudepoint create --description "Before debugging memory leak"
207	
208	# 2. Add debug code, console logs, etc.
209	# ... debug the issue ...
210	
211	# 3. After fixing, restore clean state
212	claudepoint restore "before-debugging"
213	
214	# 4. Apply only the fix
215	# ... apply the actual fix without debug code ...
216	```
217	
218	## Integration with CI/CD
219	
220	### Pre-commit Hook
221	
222	Add to `.git/hooks/pre-commit`:
223	
224	```bash
225	#!/bin/bash
226	claudepoint create --description "Pre-commit checkpoint: $(git log -1 --pretty=%B)"
227	```
228	
229	### GitHub Actions
230	
231	```yaml
232	- name: Create checkpoint before deployment
233	  run: |
234	    npm install -g claudepoint
235	    claudepoint setup
236	    claudepoint create --description "Pre-deployment checkpoint"
237	```
238	
239	## Roadmap & Future Features
240	
241	### Planned Enhancements
242	
243	- **Post-Edit Checkpoints**: Automatic checkpoints after Claude finishes editing
244	- **Smart Batching**: Group rapid changes into single checkpoint
245	- **Checkpoint Tagging**: Label by feature/bug/refactor type
246	- **Selective Restoration**: Restore specific files only
247	- **Checkpoint Comparison**: Visual diff between checkpoints
248	- **Cloud Sync**: Direct S3/cloud storage integration
249	
250	### Hook Evolution
251	
252	Future hook triggers:
253	- `after_edit_completion` - After Claude finishes editing
254	- `after_successful_tests` - When tests pass
255	- `before_git_commit` - Git workflow integration
256	- `session_milestones` - Periodic session checkpoints
257	
258	## Pro Tips
259	
260	1. **Combine with Git**: Use ClaudePoint for rapid experimentation, Git for permanent history
261	2. **Name conventions**: Use prefixes like `feature/`, `fix/`, `experiment/`
262	3. **Regular snapshots**: Force full checkpoints at major milestones
263	4. **Clean as you go**: Periodically review and clean old checkpoints
264	5. **Document changes**: Use the changelog feature extensively
265	
266	## Debugging ClaudePoint
267	
268	Enable debug output:
269	
270	```bash
271	# Unix/macOS
272	DEBUG=1 claudepoint create
273	
274	# Windows
275	set DEBUG=1 && claudepoint create
276	```
277	
278	Check MCP communication:
279	
280	```bash
281	echo '{"method": "initialize"}' | claudepoint
282	```
283	
284	## File Format Details
285	
286	### Manifest Structure
287	
288	Each checkpoint's `manifest.json`:
289	
290	```json
291	{
292	  "name": "checkpoint_name",
293	  "timestamp": "ISO 8601 timestamp",
294	  "description": "User description",
295	  "type": "FULL|INCREMENTAL",
296	  "files": ["array", "of", "files"],
297	  "fileCount": 100,
298	  "totalSize": 1048576,
299	  "fileHashes": {
300	    "file.js": "sha256hash..."
301	  },
302	  "baseCheckpoint": "parent_checkpoint_name",
303	  "changes": {
304	    "added": ["new.js"],
305	    "modified": ["existing.js"],
306	    "deleted": ["old.js"]
307	  },
308	  "statistics": {
309	    "filesChanged": 3,
310	    "bytesAdded": 1024,
311	    "bytesModified": 2048
312	  }
313	}
314	```
315	
316	### Changelog Format
317	
318	The `.checkpoints/changelog.json`:
319	
320	```json
321	[
322	  {
323	    "timestamp": "ISO 8601 timestamp",
324	    "action": "CREATE_CHECKPOINT|RESTORE_CHECKPOINT|CUSTOM",
325	    "description": "What happened",
326	    "details": "Additional context"
327	  }
328	]
329	```

